--- !u!114 &924587104
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 924587102}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 0
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "<color=#5CCCFF>\xBB</color>  <b>Runtime API:</b> magnet.SetStrength /
    SetMode / enabled / OnModeChanged; pad.SetImpulseForce / ApplyImpulseToObject(go)
    / OnImpulseApplied; mine.Explode() / Explode(force) / OnExplode / OnObjectAffected.\n<color=#5CCCFF>\xBB</color> 
    <b>Scene workflow:</b> [Demo] World: Magnet (MagneticField, Toggle 2.2 s pull
    / 0.45 s push), Impulse Field (trigger BoxCollider + ImpulseZone, Custom up,
    over an elastic Bounce Plate), Mine (ExplosiveForce, Manual). The card's controls
    call these components directly.\n<color=#5CCCFF>\xBB</color>  <b>Verification:</b>
    Play: the magnet pulses on its own; the field speeds the balls up on the way
    up and slows them on the way down, so they keep bouncing (Kick revives a ball
    that stopped). Detonate and Mega blast throw the crates; restart Play to restack
    them.\n<color=#5CCCFF>\xBB</color>  Strength slider \u203A MagneticField.SetStrength
    (dynamic float)\n<color=#5CCCFF>\xBB</color>  Kick the balls \u203A ImpulseZone.ApplyImpulseToObject(ball)\n<color=#5CCCFF>\xBB</color> 
    Mega blast \u203A ExplosiveForce.Explode(18)"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2180264, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
